### TypeScript Lint Handling
**For strict TypeScript linters that reject `as any`:**

**✅ WORKING approach (suppresses linter warnings):**
```typescript
// Mock the module with implementation
jest.mock('@/hooks/useAuth', () => ({
  useAuth: jest.fn(),
}));

// This pattern avoids TypeScript issues
const mockUseAuth = useAuth as jest.MockedFunction<typeof useAuth>;
```

**❌ AVOID approach (causes linter errors):**
```typescript
login: jest.fn() as any,  // Linter rejects this
```

